  The article says the gaurs camp in Ayyarpadi Upperparai estate, but the draft's headline and slides say 'Ayyarpadi estate' generally; the reel_script's 'ரொட்டிக்கடை செல்லும் வழியில் உள்ள அய்யர்பாடி அப்பர்பாரளை எஸ்டேட்' conflates the location (article: Ayyarpadi estate is on the Rottikadai road, while Upperparai is the sub-area where the gaurs camp) — the reel_script and slide 2 present the Rottikadai road as the location of Upperparai, a slight conflation of two places.
  Slide 2 ('எங்கே?') states that 'யானை, சிறுத்தை, கரடி உள்ளிட்ட வனவிலங்குகளும் காணப்படுகின்றன' as a fact, and the reel_script's 'பகல் நேரத்தில்' attribution for these animals is accurate, but the caption adds 'காட்டுமாடு' to the list of animals seen during the day, which is consistent with the article; no error there.
  The reel_script says the forest department 'எஸ்டேட் நிர்வாகங்களுக்கு அறிவுறுத்தியுள்ளனர்' (instructed estate managements), while the article quotes officials saying estate managements 'should not' deploy workers — the instruction is accurately conveyed, but the slide 'வனவிலங்குகள் இருந்தால் தொழிலாளர்களை பணியில்' is an incomplete, ungrammatical sentence with no clear meaning in Tamil.
  Slide 3 line 'எஸ்டேட் நிர்வாகங்கள் கவனிக்க வேண்டும்' ('estate managements should pay attention') is an invented paraphrase not stated in the article, which says estate managements should not engage workers when wild animals are present.
